# Agent & LLM Instructions — Vesta Engineering Conventions

> **Purpose.** This file is the canonical engineering guide for **Vesta** (`com.vesta.desktop`):
> a modular Rust Cargo workspace (`core/*`, `lib/*`, `cli/*`, `apps/srt-gui`, `apps/whisper-bench`)
> built with **Tauri v2 + Svelte 5 (Runes) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4**.
> Read alongside [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md), [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), and
> [`docs/QUALITY.md`](docs/QUALITY.md). Treat every rule below as mandatory unless explicitly overridden.

---

## 0. Golden Rules

1. **Never hardcode colors.** Use the semantic CSS variables in `apps/srt-gui/src/app.css` (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--surface-3`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--accent`, `--accent-strong`, `--accent-text`, `--done`, `--danger`, `--control-*`, `--glass-*`) or Tailwind tokens mapped to them.
2. **No raw browser defaults.** Never use native `<select>`, unstyled `<input type="checkbox">`, raw system scrollbars where custom ones apply, or unguarded native file dialogs. Use shared components (`SearchableSelect.svelte`, `ConfirmDialog.svelte`, `AppContextMenu.svelte`, `AppTooltip.svelte`, `dialogGuard.ts`).
3. **One source of truth per concern.**
   - Version → [`build-scripts/PKGBUILD`](build-scripts/PKGBUILD) `pkgver` (propagated by `build-scripts/update_project_info.sh`).
   - Heavy domain logic → pure Rust crates in `core/*` and `lib/*` (never duplicated in Tauri handlers or Svelte).
   - Persisted UI state/settings → [`apps/srt-gui/src/lib/config/vestaConfig.ts`](apps/srt-gui/src/lib/config/vestaConfig.ts) (never raw `localStorage`).
   - Translations → `apps/srt-gui/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json` + lazy-loaded per-language JSONs (15 languages).
   - Code/doc alignment → [`docs/contracts_manifest.json`](docs/contracts_manifest.json) checked by `build-scripts/check_doc_contracts.py`.
4. **Keep engines decoupled from Tauri and GUI.** `core/*` and `lib/*` crates must remain headless-ready, callback/cancellation-driven, and consumable by `cli/*`, `vesta-mcp`, and `apps/srt-gui/src-tauri`.
5. **Commit language & style.** Write all commit subjects, bodies, Rust errors, logs, and code comments in **English** using Conventional Commits (§14).
6. **Verify before declaring done.** Run the appropriate verification gates (`quality_check.py`, `check_doc_contracts.py`, `cargo clippy`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, i18n checks — see §16).
7. **Accessibility and RTL are mandatory.** Keyboard handlers on all custom controls, visible focus states, logical CSS properties where layout direction matters, and `dir="rtl"` support for Arabic (`ar`).

---

## 1. Tech Stack & Frontend Conventions

### 1.1 Backend & Frameworks
- **Workspace**: Rust edition `2024`, `rust-version = "1.99"`, resolver `"3"`.
- **Desktop shell**: **Tauri v2** (`tauri 2.12`) in `apps/srt-gui/src-tauri` (GPL-3.0-only).
- **Frontend**: **Svelte 5** (`^5.55`) + **TypeScript** (`^6.0`) + **Vite 8** (`port: 5175`, `strictPort: true`).
  - Note `svelteVirtualCssFallback()` in `apps/srt-gui/vite.config.ts` — keep it intact so HMR/cold virtual `<style>` modules never fall back to raw `.svelte` source under `@tailwindcss/vite`.
- **CSS**: **Tailwind CSS v4** (`@import "tailwindcss";` in `apps/srt-gui/src/app.css`) combined with semantic CSS variables and shared semantic utility classes (`.glass-card`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-icon`, `.btn-compact`, `.btn-success`, `.btn-danger`, `.input-modern`, `.vesta-context-menu`, `.searchable-select-*`, `.progress-modern*`).

### 1.2 Svelte 5 Runes & Module Conventions
- Use **Svelte 5 runes** (`$state`, `$derived`, `$props()`, `$effect`) and snippets (`{#snippet}`) consistently across components and `*.svelte.ts` stores. Do not mix Svelte 4 `export let` / `$:` syntax with runes in the same file.
- Frontend orchestration and pure workflow logic belong in `apps/srt-gui/src/lib/workflows/*.ts` (with unit tests `*.test.ts` and injected IPC callbacks) rather than bloating `.svelte` templates.
- All Tauri IPC calls go through `$lib/services/tauriClient.ts` (`invokeCommand`) so support logging, error normalization, and test mocking stay centralized.
- **Static AST guard (`npm run check:patterns`)**: `apps/srt-gui/scripts/check-code-patterns.mjs` parses `.ts` and `.svelte` scripts and rejects `debugger` statements, `new Promise(async ...)`, and `array.forEach(async ...)`. Never introduce those patterns.

---

## 2. Design Tokens & CSS Architecture (`apps/srt-gui/src/app.css`)

Vesta uses a dark-first glassmorphic theme driven by CSS custom properties in `:root` (`color-scheme: dark;`):
- **Core surfaces & text**: `--bg` (`--color-gray-950`), `--surface` (`--color-gray-800`), `--surface-2` (`--color-gray-900`), `--surface-3` (`--color-gray-700`), `--text` (`--color-gray-100`), `--muted` (`--color-gray-400`), `--border` (`--glass-border`).
- **Accents & status**: `--accent` (`--color-indigo-500`), `--accent-strong` (`--color-indigo-600`), `--accent-text` (`--color-white`), `--done` (`--color-emerald-300`), `--danger` (`--color-red-400`).
- **Controls & menus**: `--control-bg`, `--control-hover-bg`, `--control-focus-bg`, `--control-border`, `--control-focus-border`, `--control-menu-bg` (opaque `#18212e` so dropdown lists never bleed into background content), `--control-option-hover`, `--control-option-highlight`, `--control-option-selected`.
- **Glass & gradients**: `--glass-bg`, `--glass-border`, `--shadow`, `--shadow-glow`, `--gradient-primary`, `--gradient-secondary`, `--gradient-success`, `--gradient-dark`.
- **Scroll performance in Settings**: Inside `.settings-scroll`, `.glass-card` deliberately disables `backdrop-filter` and sets `contain: layout paint style` + `content-visibility: auto` to prevent Chromium continuous repainting during scroll. Preserve this optimization.

---

## 3. Repository & Directory Architecture

```text
vesta/
├─ Cargo.toml                           # [workspace] members: core/*, lib/*, cli/*, apps/srt-gui/src-tauri, apps/whisper-bench/src-tauri
├─ Cargo.lock                           # committed; kept in sync at release
├─ .cargo/config.toml                   # sets WHISPER_DONT_GENERATE_BINDINGS = "1"
├─ core/                                # Foundational zero-UI crates
│  ├─ srt-parser/                       # SRT parser/writer, auto-charset detection, atomic persistence
│  ├─ srt-apkg/                         # Native Anki .apkg ZIP + SQLite collection builder/extractor
│  └─ srt-download/                     # Cancellable downloads & atomic publication
├─ lib/                                 # Headless domain engines (CancellationToken + callbacks, zero Tauri deps)
│  ├─ srt-flashcards/                   # Anki deck compiler & bounded FFmpeg media export
│  ├─ srt-translate/                    # Multi-tier LLM translator with failover
│  ├─ srt-transcribe/                   # Local Whisper (whisper-rs) + Silero/WebRTC VAD + cloud STT
│  ├─ srt-autosync/                     # VAD + Whisper speech auto-alignment
│  ├─ srt-extract/                      # Media & subtitle track extractor
│  ├─ srt-ocr/                          # Bitmap & hardcoded ROI subtitle OCR
│  ├─ srt-refine/                       # LLM deck annotation & enrichment
│  ├─ srt-sync/                         # Anchor-based retiming engine & undo history
│  └─ srt-ankiconnect/                  # AnkiConnect HTTP client
├─ cli/                                 # Headless CLIs + stdio MCP server
│  ├─ vesta-cli/                        # Unified CLI dispatcher
│  ├─ vesta-mcp/                        # Local stdio MCP server (rmcp, 12 tools)
│  └─ srt-*-cli/                        # 8 per-engine CLIs
├─ apps/
│  ├─ srt-gui/                          # Tauri v2 + Svelte 5 desktop app (`vesta`, Vite port 5175)
│  │  ├─ package.json                   # frontend deps & scripts (`check`, `test`, `check:patterns`, `check:i18n`, `test:dev-css`)
│  │  ├─ scripts/                       # i18n audit/split/merge, check-code-patterns, check-dev-css
│  │  ├─ src/
│  │  │  ├─ main.ts                     # startup sequence (hydrates vestaConfig -> initI18n -> mounts App)
│  │  │  ├─ App.svelte                  # outer shell, lazy tab loaders, global shortcut & drag/drop handling
│  │  │  ├─ app.css                     # Tailwind v4 + design tokens + shared component classes
│  │  │  └─ lib/
│  │  │     ├─ components/              # Sidebar, FooterActions, SearchableSelect, Snackbar, ShortcutOverlay, AppContextMenu, PluginRenderer, …
│  │  │     ├─ config/vestaConfig.ts    # synchronous cache + serialized Tauri disk persistence
│  │  │     ├─ i18n/                    # index.ts + locales/*.json (15 languages)
│  │  │     ├─ modals/                  # ConfirmDialog, FirstRunSetupModal, FlashcardsPreviewModal, SupportModal, …
│  │  │     ├─ panels/                  # Modular feature & settings panels
│  │  │     ├─ services/                # tauriClient, tauriHttp, pluginClient, modelCatalog, modelDiscovery, …
│  │  │     ├─ stores/                  # *.svelte.ts runes stores (snackbarStore, uiModeStore, aiStore, ankiStore, supportLogStore, …)
│  │  │     ├─ tabs/                    # Lazy-loaded tabs (Flashcards, Refine, Translate, Sync, Align, Transcribe, Extract, Experimental, Settings, Plugins, ShortcutsTab)
│  │  │     ├─ types/                   # Shared TS types
│  │  │     ├─ utils/                   # dialogGuard, shortcuts, shortcutSearch, supportLog, tabLoader, windowLifecycle, …
│  │  │     └─ workflows/               # Pure/testable frontend workflow orchestration + *.test.ts
│  │  └─ src-tauri/                     # Tauri composition root (`commands/`, `plugins/`, `media_stream.rs`, `media_range.rs`, `state.rs`)
│  └─ whisper-bench/                    # Whisper.cpp & VAD benchmarking utility
├─ vendor/whisper-rs-sys-0.15.0/        # Patched FFI crate pinned via [patch.crates-io]
