## 4. Startup Invariant, Shell & Tab Layout

### 4.1 Critical Startup Order (`apps/srt-gui/src/main.ts`)
Many Svelte 5 stores (`aiStore`, `ankiStore`, `uiMode`, `i18n`, …) are module-level singletons whose `$state(vestaConfig.getItem(...))` runs at **module evaluation time**.
- `main.ts` MUST `await hydrateVestaConfig()` **before** dynamically importing `$lib/i18n` (`await initI18n()`) and `./App.svelte`.
- **Never** convert `./App.svelte` or store/i18n imports in `main.ts` into static top-level imports, or singleton stores will initialize against an empty config cache.

### 4.2 Outer Shell & Lazy Tabs (`apps/srt-gui/src/App.svelte`)
- Outer `<main>` uses `flex h-screen min-w-[460px] min-h-[520px] bg-gray-900 text-gray-100`, containing `Sidebar.svelte` and a `flex-1 overflow-hidden relative` workspace container.
- Built-in tabs: `flashcards` and `extract` are eager; `refine`, `translate`, `sync`, `align`, `transcribe`, `experimental`, `settings`, and `plugins` (which also handles dynamic `plugin:<id>` routes) are lazy-loaded via `tabLoaders` + `createTabLoader` and preloaded via `preloadTabs` / sidebar hover.
- Loaded tabs stay mounted and toggle visibility via `class:hidden={activeTab !== ...}` to preserve in-progress state across tab switches.

### 4.3 Workspace & Footer Band (`FooterActions.svelte`)
- Standard full-height tabs use a `.tab-layout flex flex-col h-full` structure with a single inner scroll container (`min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto`) and a fixed bottom action band via **`FooterActions.svelte`** (`h-[92px]` or `min-h-[92px]` when `wrap` is true, `border-t border-white/10 bg-gray-900`, `left`/`center`/`right`/`background` snippets).
- **Never** re-implement bespoke tab footer bars when `FooterActions.svelte` fits, and **never** let the outer `<main>` window scroll.
- Every flex/grid parent wrapping a scrollable child must keep `min-w-0` / `min-h-0` (or `overflow-hidden`) to prevent double scrollbars or squashed layouts.

---

## 5. UI/UX Harmony, Components & Easy/Expert Mode

- **Buttons**: `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-icon` (2rem×2rem), `.btn-compact`, `.btn-success`, `.btn-danger`.
- **Inputs & Selects**: `.input-modern` for text/number fields; **`SearchableSelect.svelte`** (`.searchable-select-input` / `.searchable-select-dropdown`) for all styled dropdowns — never raw `<select>`.
- **Context Menus & Tooltips**: **`AppContextMenu.svelte`** (`.vesta-context-menu`) and **`AppTooltip.svelte`** (`viewportTooltip.ts`).
- **Feedback & Empty States**: `EmptyState.svelte`, `LoadingSpinner.svelte`, `ProgressFill.svelte`, `ConfirmDialog.svelte`.
- **Easy vs Expert Mode (`stores/uiModeStore.svelte.ts`)**: `uiMode.expertMode` / `uiMode.easyMode` controls progressive disclosure across tabs. When disabling Expert mode, back up affected settings (e.g. export format) and restore clean Easy defaults (`.apkg`, `n-1` CPU cores, minimal decisions).
- **Modals & Accessibility**: Modals trap/manage focus, close on `Escape`, stop click propagation on the inner card over the backdrop, and provide full keyboard navigation (`Enter`/`Space` on `role="button"` toggle cards).
- **RTL**: Support Arabic (`ar`) with logical properties (`margin/padding/border-inline-start|end`, `inset-inline-start|end`) rather than physical left/right offsets where directional mirroring matters.

---

## 6. Configuration Persistence (`$lib/config/vestaConfig.ts`)

- All user preferences and persisted UI flags go through `vestaConfig.getItem` / `setItem` / `removeItem` / `flush`.
- `vestaConfig` hydrates an in-memory cache from Tauri at startup and serializes writes through `config_set` / `config_remove` / `config_replace_all` on disk (`vesta_config.json`), keeping reads synchronous for Svelte 5 stores while remaining crash-safe.
- Call `await vestaConfig.flush()` before reloading or completing critical setup/import flows.

---

## 7. i18n & Localization (15 Languages, On-Demand Chunks)

- **Supported languages (15)**: `ar` (RTL), `zh`, `nl`, `en`, `fr`, `de`, `hi`, `it`, `ja`, `ko`, `pl`, `pt`, `ru`, `es`, `tr` in `apps/srt-gui/src/lib/i18n/locales/*.json`.
- **Lazy chunk loading (`apps/srt-gui/src/lib/i18n/index.ts`)**: Only `en.json` is statically bundled in the main JS chunk; all other locales are loaded on demand via `import.meta.glob('./locales/*.json')` and merged as `{ ...en, ...dict }`, guaranteeing fallback to English rather than raw keys.
- **Store API**: Use `let t = $derived($locale);` in Svelte components, with `{{paramName}}` interpolation. When `currentLanguage` is `'ar'`, set `document.documentElement.dir = 'rtl'` (else `'ltr'`).
- **Strict audit gates**:
  - `bash build-scripts/check-i18n.sh`
  - `npm run check:i18n` (in `apps/srt-gui`)
  - `python3 apps/srt-gui/scripts/check_missing_translations.py --fail-on-issues`
  - Keep all 15 locale JSON files in sync whenever adding or renaming keys in `en.json`.

---

## 8. Keyboard Shortcuts Engine & `ShortcutsTab.svelte`

- Defaults, normalization, formatting, conflict detection (`shortcutsShareScope`), and reserved-key checks (`isReservedShortcut`) live in `apps/srt-gui/src/lib/utils/shortcuts.ts` (`defaultShortcuts`, persisted via `vestaConfig`).
- Global key listeners must ignore events coming from `INPUT`, `TEXTAREA`, or `contentEditable` elements (`isInputActive` in `utils/keyboardFocus.ts`).
- `ShortcutsTab.svelte` provides category filtering, per-row rebind/reset, reset-all confirmation, and dual-mode search (`text` vs live `keys` capture via `utils/shortcutSearch.ts`). Always register new user-facing shortcuts in `defaultShortcuts` with localized `description` keys and show them in `ShortcutOverlay.svelte` / `ShortcutsTab.svelte`.

---

## 9. Snackbars & Notifications (`stores/snackbarStore.svelte.ts` + `Snackbar.svelte`)

- Use the singleton `snackbar` from `$lib/stores/snackbarStore.svelte`.
- Default duration is `SNACKBAR_DEFAULT_DURATION = 1700` ms, automatically raised to a minimum of `3500` ms for `warning` and `5000` ms for `error`.
- Concurrent messages coalesce duplicates and queue up to `SNACKBAR_MAX_PENDING = 8`; hovering/focusing pauses the timer via `pause(reason)` / `resume(reason)`.

---

## 10. Native Dialog Guard (`$lib/utils/dialogGuard.ts`)

- Never call `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog`'s `open` or `save` directly (concurrent calls can freeze or crash native dialog portals).
- Always use `guardedOpen` / `guardedSave`, which enforce an in-flight lock, record `dialog.open` / `dialog.done` / `dialog.error` support telemetry, and return `null` if a dialog is already open. Callers must handle `null` gracefully.

---

## 11. Sidebar, Attribution Dock, Inbox & Support (`Sidebar.svelte`)

- Bottom-left footer (`h-[92px]`) displays:
  - Cached local avatar (`src/assets/avatar.png` → `https://pierspad.com`)
  - Current version button (opens `NotificationInbox.svelte`, combining settings action notices and update availability via `updateCheckerStore.svelte.ts`)
  - License link (`GPL-3.0`)
  - Sponsor/Support button (`SupportModal.svelte`) and GitHub repository icon link (`https://github.com/pierspad/vesta`)
- Collapsed sidebar centers the repo icon cleanly. Clicking the brand logo 7 times within 4 seconds unlocks the `experimental` tab (`vesta-experimental-unlocked` in `vestaConfig`).

---

## 12. Whisper Integration (`lib/srt-transcribe` + `vendor/whisper-rs-sys-0.15.0`)

- Audio/speech transcription is centralized in `lib/srt-transcribe` (shared by `srt-transcribe-cli`, `srt-autosync`, `vesta-mcp`, and `apps/srt-gui`). Never duplicate Whisper FFI/model logic in Tauri commands or other crates.
- **Vendored build fix (`vendor/whisper-rs-sys-0.15.0/`)**:
  - Pinned via `[patch.crates-io]` in root `Cargo.toml` so `whisper-rs-sys` explicitly links all split GGML static libraries (`whisper`, `ggml`, `ggml-base`, `ggml-cpu`).
  - `.cargo/config.toml` sets `WHISPER_DONT_GENERATE_BINDINGS = "1"`, and `.github/workflows/bindgen-drift-check.yml` guards against bindgen drift. Re-verify link directives and bindings if bumping `whisper-rs`.
- **GPU offload & fallback**:
  - `srt-transcribe` exposes optional Cargo features `vulkan`, `cuda`, `rocm`, `sycl`.
  - Linux desktop builds in `apps/srt-gui/src-tauri/Cargo.toml` enable `vulkan` by default (`srt-transcribe/vulkan`, `srt-autosync/vulkan`); runtime selection (`TranscriptionConfig::use_gpu`) still falls back safely to CPU if no usable Vulkan device exists.
- **Module responsibilities in `lib/srt-transcribe/src/`**:
  - `audio.rs` / `audio/`: FFmpeg extraction to 16 kHz mono `pcm_s16le` WAV, draining stderr asynchronously to prevent pipe deadlocks, respecting `CancellationToken`.
  - `model.rs`: Whisper/VAD model catalog, `.partial` atomic downloads, throttled progress callbacks.
  - `transcribe.rs` & `webrtc.rs`: `whisper.cpp` inference + Silero/WebRTC VAD span segmentation, physical-core thread defaults, centisecond→millisecond timestamp conversion.
  - `cloud.rs` & `pipeline.rs`: Cloud STT endpoints and unified transcription orchestration.

---

## 13. Headless Engines, MCP, Plugin SDK & Contract Enforcement

- **Pure domain crates**: `core/*` and `lib/*` accept `CancellationToken` + progress/diagnostic callbacks and never import Tauri or initialize global loggers.
- **MCP server (`cli/vesta-mcp`)**: Uses `rmcp` over stdio exposing the 12 documented tools (`get_configuration`, `inspect_subtitles`, `preview_flashcards`, `generate_flashcards`, `translate_subtitles`, `transcribe_media`, `list_embedded_subtitles`, `ocr_subtitles`, `get_job`, `cancel_job`, `list_plugins`, `call_plugin`) with path-root and credential isolation.
- **Declarative Plugin SDK**: Subprocess JSON-RPC stdio plugins rendered by `PluginRenderer.svelte` and validated with `docs/examples/plugin-hello/vesta_plugin.py` (`init`, `validate`, `test`).
- **Contract verification (`build-scripts/check_doc_contracts.py`)**: Keep `docs/contracts_manifest.json` and `docs/**/*.md` synchronized whenever modifying:
  1. Tauri IPC commands (`apps/srt-gui/src-tauri/src/main.rs` / `commands/`)
  2. MCP tools (`cli/vesta-mcp/src/lib.rs` vs `docs/MCP.md`)
  3. CLI crates and subcommand flags (`cli/*/src/*.rs` vs `docs/modules/*.md`)
  4. Plugin SDK widget builders (`PluginRenderer.svelte` vs `vesta_plugin.py` and `docs/PLUGINS.md`)
  5. Public Rust API signatures/fields in `core/*` and `lib/*` vs `docs/modules/*.md`
  6. Markdown links and heading anchors across docs

---

## 14. Versioning & Release-Notes Governance

- **Single source of truth**: `build-scripts/PKGBUILD` `pkgver`. Never hand-edit version numbers or create git tags manually.
- `build-scripts/update_project_info.sh` propagates `pkgver` to `apps/srt-gui/package.json`, `tauri.conf.json`, `Cargo.toml` (`[workspace.package]` & internal path pins), `.desktop`/Flatpak manifests, and `Cargo.lock`.
- `build-scripts/check_internal_crate_versions.sh` enforces full consistency across workspace crates and `Cargo.lock`.
- **Commit style**: English Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `perf:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`, `build:`). Keep subjects clear for end-user release notes (generated by `semantic-release`). Keep bodies empty or at most 1–3 concise lines explaining non-obvious root causes or tradeoffs — no AI-style multi-bullet dumps.

---

## 15. CI, Build & Release Workflows (`.github/workflows/`)

- **`ci.yml`**: Runs on push (`main`, `dev`) and PRs — checks Tauri version compatibility, release workflow tests, doc contracts, frontend (`check`, `test`, `test:dev-css`, `check:i18n`, `build`), strict `cargo clippy --locked --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, workspace tests, and internal crate versions (with `sccache`).
- **`bindgen-drift-check.yml`**: Verifies vendored `whisper-rs-sys` bindings stay valid.
- **`release.yml`**: Runs `semantic-release` on `main` (stable) and `dev` (prerelease), updates `PKGBUILD` + project versions + `Cargo.lock`, tags, creates the release, dispatches `build.yml`, and backmerges `main` → `dev`.
- **`build.yml` & `build-arm64.yml`**: Build Linux `.deb`, `.rpm`, Arch, Flatpak, Windows x64/ARM64 installers (with `smoke-windows-arm64`), and macOS ARM64 `.dmg`.
- **`aur-publish.yml`**: Publishes stable releases to AUR (`vesta-bin`) via `build-scripts/ci-push-aur.sh`.
- **`whisper-bench.yml`**: Tracks Whisper/VAD benchmarks via `apps/whisper-bench`.

---

## 16. Verification Gates & Definition of Done

Before considering work complete:
1. **Frontend changes** (in `apps/srt-gui`):
   - `npm run check` (`svelte-check`)
   - `npm test` (runs `test:merge`, `test:glob`, `check:patterns` AST gate, and `vitest run`)
   - `npm run test:dev-css`
   - If UI strings changed: update `en.json` and all 14 other locales, then run `npm run check:i18n` and `bash ../../build-scripts/check-i18n.sh`
2. **Rust / IPC / CLI / MCP / Plugin changes** (from repo root):
   - `cargo fmt --all --check`
   - `cargo clippy --locked --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` (or targeted crates while iterating, full workspace before finish)
   - `python3 build-scripts/check_doc_contracts.py` (run `--report` to inspect drift; `--update` only after intentional documented API/IPC/CLI/MCP/SDK updates)
   - `python3 build-scripts/check_library_integration.py`
3. **Full pre-PR / pre-release gate**:
   - `python3 build-scripts/quality_check.py` (fast headless gate)
   - `python3 build-scripts/quality_check.py --desktop --smoke` (full gate including native `vesta` crate and synthetic FFmpeg/APKG smoke test)
